 when Vesper and Robin won their matches and Bajkó had a bye. This made them the finalists, but no matches were necessary as Vesper had already beaten Robin, and drawn with Bajkó, and Robin had defeated Bajkó, giving the gold medal to Vesper, with Robin winning his second silver medal in 1968 wrestling. Robin’s two medals made him one of only 13 Olympic wrestlers to win medals in both styles at the Olympics, and one of only two, along with Swede " [:a {:href "/athletes/60134"} "Rudolf Svensson"] " in 1924, to win two silver medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "21"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58317"} "Rudolf Vesper"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58128"} "Daniel Robin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "20"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58542"} "Károly Bajkó"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "10"] [:td {} [:a